# Right Age to Start Preschool: A Simple Parent Guide

Your neighbour’s child started at two. Your cousin says three is better. The school says “anytime.” What is the right age to start preschool?

There’s no single number, but there are clear signs, and this guide explains them in plain words.

**Disclosure:** This guide is published by [Thames Valley Preschool](https://thamesvalleyglobal.org/), a preschool brand. We’ve kept the advice general so it works for any school.

## How Do You Know the Right Age to Start Preschool?

Many Indian children start play school between about 2 and 3 years and nursery at around 3. The right age for your child is when they can manage a few hours away from you in a safe, friendly place.

A number on the calendar matters less than how your child feels.

Children develop at different speeds. A confident two-and-a-half-year-old may be ready earlier than a shy three-year-old. That’s normal, and it doesn’t predict how they’ll do later.

## Key Takeaway

Preschool readiness depends on a child's individual development, comfort, and ability to adjust to a new environment—not just their age.

